---
title: Coffee, Cocoa and Raisin Loaf
source: https://www.siemens-home.bsh-group.com/uk/en/c/recipe/blt9ea0f45f353090f4/indulgent-coffee-cocoa-and-raisin-loaf
course: Side
prep time: 1h
cook time: 50m
locale: en
difficulty: Hard
---

= Poolish (yeast pre-ferment) =

For the poolish, mix the @strong white flour{100%g}, @malted (granary) flour{100%g}, @fast acting dried yeast{3.5%g}, and @water{250%ml} in a large bowl. Leave at room temperature for 12 to ~poolish{24%hours}.

= Espresso Raisins =

Let the @espresso{180%ml}(2 × espresso doppio) cool slightly, and then add sufficient @raisins{200%g} until just covered. Leave to soak for 12 to ~raisins{24%hours}.

= Dough =

The next day, for the dough mix together the @strong white flour{450%g}, @malted (granary) flour{180%g}, @cocoa powder{40%g}(sieved), @salt{12%g}, and @fast acting dried yeast{3.5%g}, until combined. Add the poolish and 200 ml of the @water{300%ml} (but not the espresso soaked raisins). Knead on a low speed for about ~{5%minutes} until a smooth dough starts to form. Add the soaked raisins, and (if necessary) some of the remaining water. Knead for a further ~{3%minutes} until smooth.

Transfer to a clean bowl and place in a warm place (e.g. oven set to 35°C) for ~{30%minutes} or until doubled in size.

Turn the dough out onto an un-floured surface and knock back slightly. Lightly dust the top with @rice flour{} and turn over. Shape into a boule by folding each corner into the centre to create a seam. Then turn the dough over, using a bench scraper to help rotate the dough around to create surface tension.

Line a clean bowl with a tea towel and generously dust with @rice flour{}. Place the shaped loaf into this bowl and leave to rise for a further ~{25%minutes} until doubled in size again.

Preheat the oven to 220°C with a #universal pan{} set at level 2, and a dish of water on the base of the oven. Once preheated, turn the risen loaf onto a piece of baking parchment over a #pizza peel{}. Score the top of the loaf with a serrated knife, to create the “ear” of the loaf.

Carefully slide the loaf onto the preheated tray and reduce the oven temperature to 180°C. Bake for 40 to ~{50%minutes} until golden and the loaf sounds hollow when tapped on the base.